  "id": "khmer_mohori",
  "name": "Mohori (Khmer entertainment ensemble)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Khmer entertainment ensemble, played at the royal court for banquets and dance and in towns and villages for festivities, with sung texts on love and nature. It combines the roneat xylophone, the tro sau and tro u fiddles, the krapeu crocodile zither, flute, small drums and chhing cymbals with a singer. After the Khmer Rouge period the repertoire was rebuilt and taught by the Royal University of Fine Arts.",
  "recipe": "classic modern mohori, art Music, southeast Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, seven equal 171 cent steps. royal court pinpeat canonical pre 1975 lineage roneat ek, tro sau, coconut shell threaded between strings intimate chamber tro u, krapeu, skor daey, khmer string ensemble ching. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
